Z||000000||sqoach||10-22-2001||11:59 AM||||[RANT]<BR>#^!*#&!()*#^&@()%*!!!!!!!<P>Arrgggggggghh!!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Was getting ready to take my SE to get it aligned, when I noticed a small puddle under the front. Saw a drip. Sh!t! Looked under there and it dripped again. Green...antifreeze...damn!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"> Didn't see where it could be leaking down to there, so I'm guessing there's a hole in the bottom. The leak got worse when I took it up to the shop, and then I couldn't get it aligned because I need inner tie rods! AHHHHHHHH!!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>[END RANT]<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">               <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||NEPTUNE||10-22-2001||12:06 PM||||I recently had the same problem. Turned out to be the plastic tank on drivers side. I took the car to the radiator shop, they replaced the tank, pressure tested complete system, and pressure cleaned the radiator for $150. If I had pulled the radiator myself it would have been $75. Mine has auto and a/c. <BR>LOL.||||reg||1
